Here is the commit message:
fix kill-status bug from 2ae7c831

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by an incorrect condition in the `terminate_pid_and_wait` function that checked the process status. The original code used `if(!kill(pid, 0))`, which incorrectly interpreted the return value of `kill`. This logic meant that if the process was not running, it would enter the block, leading to unintended behavior. The corrected condition `if(kill(pid, 0))` properly checks if the process is still active, thereby fixing the logical flow and accurately handling the termination status.

Here is the patch:
 // True retval indicates daemon is still running
 static bool terminate_pid_and_wait(pid_t pid) {
     dmn_assert(pid); // don't try to kill (0, ...)

     bool still_running = false;

     if(!kill(pid, SIGTERM)) {
         still_running = true;
         struct timeval tv;
         unsigned tries = 150;
         while(tries--) {
             tv.tv_sec = 0;
             tv.tv_usec = 100000;
             select(0, NULL, NULL, NULL, &tv);
-            if(!kill(pid, 0)) {
+            if(kill(pid, 0)) {
                 still_running = false;
                 break;
             }
         }
     }

     return still_running;
 }



